KG42.register("clusters-2fd50279bde7fb174072edd9",{"id":"08-real_time_prices::v142-d-CL003","paper":"08-real_time_prices","label":"Size and deadline admission requirements for Nordic RP bids","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Size and deadline admission requirements for Nordic RP bids","market_meaning":"When designated entities in the existing Nordic RP market submit regulation bids, they must meet the minimum bid-size requirement and the submission deadline before the operating hour. This cluster expresses bid-entry conditions that can be implemented and checked independently.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"The scope is limited to the existing RP arrangements described in R007, and DEM is carried forward solely as a frozen source label. The minimum bid size and the proposed participation boundary for large generating units are distinct conditions; these bid-submission requirements do not apply to EcoGrid's bid-free participation.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The submitting entities, size conditions, submission activities, and deadline obligations already form an independent procedural rule, so a single-chain cluster is retained. It provides a shared external interface to v142-d-CL002 and is not merged into EcoGrid's submission-exemption rules merely because they share the bidding.supply identifier.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides both RP bid-size and deadline conditions, sufficient to constitute a candidate bid-submission admission rule within a limited scope."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP012","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The bid-size threshold and deadline are retained in procedural constraints, while the dedicated node proposals for minimum bid size and RP bid submission still await approval. The absence of dedicated nodes or numerical parameters does not invalidate this procedural assembly, but it cannot yet provide a typed automated validation model.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev20","v141-b-g02-ev-07"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop05","v141-b-g02-prop-04"],"required_work":"Manually assess whether dedicated admission or bid-submission concepts are needed; if automated validation is required, a subsequent version of C should explicitly define quantity and time-point objects, keeping bid thresholds separate from entity-capacity conditions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP013","category":"unverified_source","description":"Both sources for R007 are unverified; this cluster is assembled solely from the M02 candidate evidence currently permitted for use and has not undergone independent source review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev20","v141-b-g02-ev-07"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check bid sizes, applicable entities, deadlines, and the scope of the existing arrangements, maintaining the distinction between their conditions and those of the proposed anti-arbitrage rules."}]},"rule_refs":["08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-334f35169e6933ed"]});
